{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'F8|F10|P7|AX143|interface Lookup|seriesNotDrawnSentence|noteSegments|incompleteAt|totalMixed|\"'^#'\"' docs/02-product-spec.md docs/03-plan-typescript-release.md packages/axylo/src/{core/contracts.ts,core/controller.ts,dom/figure.ts,public.ts}\"","aggregated_output":"packages/axylo/src/public.ts:210:  totalMixed: string;\npackages/axylo/src/public.ts:212:  incompleteAt: string; incompleteCount: string;\npackages/axylo/src/dom/figure.ts:47:  readonly noteSegments?: readonly NoteSegment[] | null;\npackages/axylo/src/dom/figure.ts:221:      const segments = compact ? null : model.noteSegments ?? null;\npackages/axylo/src/core/contracts.ts:257: * Stacking (spec F10). Positive and negative values accumulate on their own sides of zero.\npackages/axylo/src/core/contracts.ts:308:/** One drawn slice or legend entry of a donut (spec F8). */\npackages/axylo/src/core/contracts.ts:629:export interface Lookup {\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:1:# Phase 1b: Axylo product specification\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:7:## 1. What Axylo is\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:15:### 1.1 Why someone would choose it\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:29:### 1.2 Who it is for\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:35:### 1.3 Principles\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:46:## 2. Scope of the first release\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:48:### 2.1 Chart types\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:65:### 2.2 Workflows\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:76:### 2.3 Supported environments\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:86:## 3. Acceptance criteria: the reader's experience\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:90:### 3.1 Faithful representation\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:101:| F8 | Donut: slices keep the given order, start at 12 o'clock and run clockwise. The legend shows every slice's value and percentage as text, in slice order. A zero slice is listed without an arc; a `null` slice is listed as \"No data\". A negative value is AX120 and the chart shows its error state. With more than eight slices that have an arc (a positive value), the seven largest are drawn and the rest of those are grouped as \"Other (n)\", with AX121; zero and `null` slices never count toward the limit and are never grouped, so each stays listed on its own; the table lists every category. Shares are shown with at most one fraction digit. An all-zero donut shows the empty state. | `parts` fixture; one test per case | R7, landscape scoreboard 3.1 |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:103:| F10 | Stacks place positive and negative values on their own sides of zero, and the axis covers both totals. The readout's total is the sum when every component has the same sign; when signs are mixed it gives the positive total and the negative total, the two ends the reader sees, not their net. A missing component is drawn with zero height and the stack is marked \"incomplete\" in tooltip, table and announcements. | Property test on stacked geometry; mixed-sign and incomplete fixtures | R5 |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:107:### 3.2 Legibility\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:111:| L1 | No visible text overlaps other text or is clipped, and no label disappears without the reader being told. Remedies, in order: thin (time, date, numeric and `ordered` category axes only); wrap to at most three lines; rotate up to 45°; truncate in the middle, keeping every label distinct, with the full text in tooltip and table. If labels still do not fit, a visible note (\"Some labels hidden. See table.\") appears and AX143 suggests horizontal bars. Axylo never changes a chart's orientation on its own. | In real browsers, after fonts load: for widths 240–1,920 px and generated label sets, zero intersecting text boxes (1 px tolerance), zero text outside the figure, truncated labels pairwise distinct. Repeated with the WCAG 1.4.12 text-spacing overrides, 200% text-only zoom, and a font that loads late | R2 |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:120:### 3.3 Interaction\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:131:### 3.4 Accessibility\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:148:### 3.5 Diagnostic registry\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:173:| AX143 | Hint | Labels hidden after every remedy | Note shown to the reader |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:188:### 3.6 Type matrix\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:200:### 3.7 Compact variant\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:214:### 3.8 What the evidence will and will not show\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:218:## 4. Acceptance criteria: the developer's experience\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:226:| DX5 | Three methods change a chart: `update` changes options, `append` adds rows, `zoom` sets the view. They apply in call order. Validation and diagnostics are synchronous; drawing is deferred to the next frame; marks, labels, hit testing and the accessibility layer always switch to a new state together. `destroy()` releases everything and cancels pending work. No `resize()` exists. | Sequence tests: replace then append then zoom in one turn; a rejected `strict` update leaves the last valid chart; destroy before the frame; 1,000 create–destroy cycles show no heap growth trend (P7) | D3, R16 |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:235:## 5. Performance budgets\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:248:| P7 | Memory | Bytes owned by Axylo beyond the caller's columns for 1,000,000 points; heap trend over 1,000 create–destroy cycles | Measured after forced collection | At most 1× the size of the caller's two columns; no upward slope | Not measured in Phase 1 |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:256:## 6. Decisions and the findings behind them\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:281:## 7. Changes this revision rejected\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:290:## 8. Decisions still open\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:1:# Phase 2 plan: Axylo 1.0 in TypeScript\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:9:## 1. Public API\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:13:### 1.1 Shape\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:38:### 1.2 Data: one logical table, three forms\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:63:### 1.3 Fields\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:90:### 1.4 Common options\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:107:### 1.5 Handle and commit contract\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:130:### 1.6 Diagnostics\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:149:### 1.7 React adapter\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:167:## 2. Architecture\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:169:### 2.1 Pipeline\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:190:### 2.2 Invalidation\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:204:### 2.3 Rendering\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:216:### 2.4 Document structure\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:239:### 2.5 Repository\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:255:## 3. Milestones\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:259:### M0. Foundations (ceiling: 5 days)\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:268:### M1. A vertical slice, and the two open decisions (ceiling: 12 days)\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:284:### M2. Faithful data, on the line chart (ceiling: 8 days)\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:296:### M3. Reading the chart (ceiling: 10 days)\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:309:### M4. Accessibility, complete on the line chart (ceiling: 10 days)\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:322:### M5. Bar, area, donut, scatter and the compact variant (ceiling: 18 days)\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:336:### M6. Updates and scale (ceiling: 10 days)\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:344:- Budgets P1–P5 and P7 measured with the Phase 3 method, recalibrated once if M1's provisional values were wrong, then frozen with a written reason for each.\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:348:### M7. Distribution and documentation (ceiling: 8 days)\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:359:### M8. Release (ceiling: 10 days)\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:370:## 4. Test strategy\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:386:## 5. Risks\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:398:## 6. What waits until after 1.0\npackages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:240: *   seriesNotDrawnSentence(messages: Messages, series: string, table: boolean): string\npackages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:242:function seriesNotDrawnSentence(messages: Messages, series: string, table: boolean): string {\npackages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:926:        const text = undrawn.map(s => seriesNotDrawnSentence(m, s.label, table)).join(' ');\npackages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:1132:        noteSegments: noteShown && reader.note !== null ? [{ text: reader.note, lang: noteLangFor(currentHidden, disclosureNow()) }] : null,\npackages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:1270:    if (hidden > 0) fit.push(createDiagnostic('AX143', 'none', { field: a.resolved.x.field, count: hidden }, 'presentation'));\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
