{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n -i 'borrow|mutat|immutable|typed column' docs/03-plan-typescript-release.md packages/axylo/src/public.ts; cat packages/axylo/src/data/table.ts; sed -n '85,165p' packages/axylo/src/reader/table.ts; sed -n '68,112p' packages/axylo/test/acceptance/f-stacks.test.ts; sed -n '80,135p' packages/axylo/test/acceptance/f-donut.test.ts; sed -n '125,145p;175,211p' packages/axylo/src/diagnostics/registry.ts; sed -n '88,185p' packages/axylo/test/reader/index.test.ts; sed -n '210,350p' packages/axylo/test/lookup/scatter.test.ts\"","aggregated_output":"packages/axylo/src/public.ts:8:/** Rows as an API returns them, or typed columns for large data. Both describe the same logical table. */\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:47:// typed columns for large data; the row type is inferred from the columns\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:57:| Ownership | Row arrays are read once and never mutated. Typed columns are borrowed, not copied; the caller must not change them in place, and replaces them through `update`. |\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:59:| Missing values | Rows: `null`, or an absent key. Typed columns: `NaN` means missing and does not raise AX103. |\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:179:The **frame** is the normalized, lossless data: typed columns, a validity bitmap, dictionary-encoded categories, source-row indexes and a revision number. It is the only source for exact values. The table, the summary, keyboard navigation, tooltips and events read the frame. The **scene** is geometry for drawing and may be simplified (F5); nothing reads values back from it. The first draft derived accessibility from the scene, and two reviewers showed that a simplified drawing cannot return the samples it dropped.\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:192:Stages are cached, and the cache keys are explicit. Caching on object identity alone, as the first draft said, would miss font loads, pixel-ratio changes and in-place mutation.\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:212:**Simplified drawing.** Per device-pixel column and per contiguous run of valid samples, the stroke covers the run's minimum and maximum (F5). One rule for when it applies: more than four visible samples per device-pixel column on average. The pass over visible samples is O(visible) on typed columns and is measured separately from drawing; the vertex count is bounded by width times the number of runs, not by width alone.\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:270:- `line()` from rows and from typed columns: normalization with provenance, linear, time and date scales, DOM tick labels, resize, light and dark, `destroy`.\nimport type { RowSource } from '../core/contracts';\n\nexport type Columns = Readonly<Record<string, ArrayLike<unknown>>>;\n\nexport interface Table extends RowSource {\n  readonly length: number;\n  readonly columns: Columns | null;\n  read(row: number, field: string): unknown;\n  isColumnRow(row: number): boolean;\n  rowIndex(row: number): number;\n  hasField(field: string): boolean;\n  keys(): readonly string[];\n}\n\nconst origins = new WeakMap<Table, readonly unknown[] | Columns>();\n\nexport function sameTableData(a: Table, b: Table): boolean {\n  const origin = origins.get(a);\n  return a === b || (origin !== undefined && origin === origins.get(b) && a.length === b.length);\n}\n\nfunction record(row: unknown): Record<string, unknown> | null {\n  return row !== null && typeof row === 'object' ? row as Record<string, unknown> : null;\n}\n\nexport function rowValue(row: unknown, field: string): unknown {\n  const object = record(row);\n  return object && Object.hasOwn(object, field) ? object[field] : undefined;\n}\n\nexport function rowsTable(rows: readonly unknown[]): Table {\n  const table: Table = {\n    length: rows.length,\n    columns: null,\n    read: (row, field) => rowValue(rows[row], field),\n    rowAt: row => row >= 0 && row < rows.length && Number.isInteger(row) ? rows[row] : null,\n    isColumnRow: () => false,\n    rowIndex: row => row,\n    hasField: field => rows.some(row => {\n      const object = record(row);\n      return object !== null && Object.hasOwn(object, field);\n    }),\n    keys: () => {\n      const keys = new Set<string>();\n      for (const row of rows) for (const key of Object.keys(record(row) ?? {})) keys.add(key);\n      return [...keys];\n    },\n  };\n  origins.set(table, rows);\n  return table;\n}\n\nexport function columnsTable(columns: Columns, length: number): Table {\n  const keys = Object.keys(columns);\n  const table: Table = {\n    length,\n    columns,\n    read: (row, field) => Object.hasOwn(columns, field) ? columns[field]?.[row] : undefined,\n    rowAt: row => row >= 0 && row < length && Number.isInteger(row)\n      ? Object.fromEntries(keys.map(key => [key, columns[key]?.[row]]))\n      : null,\n    hasField: field => Object.hasOwn(columns, field),\n    isColumnRow: () => true,\n    rowIndex: row => row,\n    keys: () => keys,\n  };\n  origins.set(table, columns);\n  return table;\n}\n      if (!weights) {\n        let max = 0;\n        for (let i = 0; i < rowCount; i++) if (frame.slot[i] === SLOT_VALUE) max = Math.max(max, frame.values[i]!);\n        let scaled = 0;\n        for (let i = 0; i < rowCount; i++) if (frame.slot[i] === SLOT_VALUE) scaled += frame.values[i]! / max;\n        weights = { max, total: scaled };\n      }\n      return formatters.percent(donutRatio(value / weights.max, weights.total));\n    }\n    return {\n      caption, headers: [labels.category, withUnit(frame.valueLabel, frame.unit), labels.percentage], rowCount, pageSize: PAGE_SIZE,\n      row(i) {\n        if (!Number.isInteger(i) || i < 0 || i >= rowCount) return null;\n        const state = frame.slot[i] as SlotState;\n        const value = frame.values[i]!;\n        return [frame.labels[i]!, slotText(formatters, 0, value, state), state === SLOT_VALUE && value >= 0\n          ? writePercent(value) : messages.noData];\n      },\n      pageForX(x) { return page(readPosition(x, 'category', null, frame.labels), rowCount); },\n    };\n  }\n  if (view.kind === 'scatter') {\n    const { frame } = view;\n    const order = scatterRows(view, work);\n    let next: (() => ScatterRow | null) | null = null;\n    let nextOrdinal = -1;\n    return {\n      caption, headers: [withUnit(frame.xLabel, frame.xUnit), labels.series, withUnit(frame.yLabel, frame.yUnit)],\n      rowCount: order.count, pageSize: PAGE_SIZE,\n      row(i) {\n        if (!Number.isInteger(i) || i < 0 || i >= order.count) return null;\n        if (i !== nextOrdinal) next = order.cursor(i);\n        const at = next?.();\n        nextOrdinal = i + 1;\n        if (!at) return null;\n        const series = frame.series[at.series]!;\n        if (at.missing) return [formatters.x(series.missingX![at.index]!), series.label, messages.noData];\n        return [formatters.x(series.x[at.index]!), series.label, formatters.value(at.series, series.y[at.index]!)];\n      },\n      pageForX(x) {\n        const xPos = readPosition(x, frame.xKind, frame.timeZone);\n        return Number.isFinite(xPos) ? page(order.beforeX(xPos), order.count) : null;\n      },\n    };\n  }\n\n  const { frame, visibleSlots: { start, end }, stack } = view;\n  const rowCount = end - start;\n  return {\n    caption, headers: [withUnit(frame.xLabel, labels.xUnit ?? null), ...frame.series.map(series => withUnit(series.label, series.unit))],\n    rowCount, pageSize: PAGE_SIZE,\n    row(i) {\n      if (!Number.isInteger(i) || i < 0 || i >= rowCount) return null;\n      const at = start + i;\n      const x = formatters.x(frame.x.values[at]!);\n      return [stack?.incomplete?.[at] ? incomplete(x, messages) : x,\n        ...frame.series.map((series, s) => slotText(formatters, s, series.y[at]!, series.slot[at] as SlotState))];\n    },\n    pageForX(x) {\n      const xPos = readPosition(x, frame.x.kind, frame.x.timeZone, frame.x.categories);\n      return Number.isFinite(xPos) ? page(lowerBound(frame.x.values, xPos, start, end) - start, rowCount) : null;\n    },\n  };\n}\n      }\n    }), { numRuns: 1_000 });\n  });\n\n  it(`F10 ${type}: a missing ${kind} component has zero height and the reader is told which stack is incomplete${type === 'compact' ? ' (reading: the summary provides the incomplete warning)' : ''}`, () => {\n    const r = chart(type, [\n      { x: 1, a: 5, b: -3, c: 4, d: -2 },\n      { x: 2, a: 5, b: -3, c: null, d: -2 },\n      { x: 3, a: 5, b: -3, c: 4, d: -2 },\n    ], options(kind), undefined, kind);\n    r.frames();\n    const { x, y } = axes(r);\n    if (kind === 'bar') {\n      const missing = marks(r, 'rects').find(mark => mark.series === 2 && mark.variant === 'missing');\n      expect(missing?.xywh).toHaveLength(4);\n      expectGeometry([missing!.xywh[1]!, missing!.xywh[3]!], [y.map(5), 0]);\n    } else {\n      const mark = marks(r, 'area').find(mark => mark.series === 2)!;\n      const middle = pixel(x, 2);\n      const ordinate = (xy: Float32Array) => points(xy).filter(p => Math.abs(p[0] - middle) < 0.001);\n      expect(ordinate(mark.upper).some(p => Math.abs(p[1] - y.map(5)) < 0.001)).toBe(true);\n      expect(ordinate(mark.lower).some(p => Math.abs(p[1] - y.map(5)) < 0.001)).toBe(true);\n    }\n    if (type === 'compact') {\n      expectCompact(r);\n      expect(lastModel(r).summary).toContain('incomplete');\n    } else {\n      expect(at(r, 2).rows.map(row => row.value)).toEqual(['5', '-3', 'No data', '-2']);\n      expect(rows(r)[1]).toEqual(['2 (incomplete)', '5', '-3', 'No data', '-2']);\n      const announced = reading(r, refAt(r, 2));\n      expect(announced).toContain(defaultMessages.incompleteStack);\n      const spokenTotals = announced?.split(defaultMessages.total)[1]?.split(defaultMessages.incompleteStack)[0];\n      expect.soft(spokenTotals?.match(/-?\\d+/g)?.map(Number)).toEqual(expect.arrayContaining([5, -5]));\n      for (const [x, positive, negative] of [[1, 9, -5], [2, 5, -5]] as const) {\n        const total = at(r, x).total;\n        const totals = total?.match(/-?\\d+/g)?.map(Number);\n        expect.soft(totals, 'the mixed-sign stack readout gives both sides').toEqual(expect.arrayContaining([positive, negative]));\n      }\n      expect(lastModel(r).note).toBeNull();\n    }\n  });\n}\n    ...Array.from({ length: 6 }, (_, i) => ({ x: 'Positive ' + i, y: i + 1 })),\n    { x: 'Zero', y: 0 }, { x: 'Missing', y: null },\n  ]);\n  r.frames();\n  expect(codes(r)).toEqual([]);\n  expect(marks(r, 'arcs')[0]?.angles).toHaveLength(12);\n  expect(rows(r).slice(-2).map(row => row.slice(0, 2))).toEqual([['Zero', '0'], ['Missing', 'No data']]);\n  expect(walk(r).slice(-2).map(ref => committed(r).lookup.datum(ref)?.seriesLabel)).toEqual(['Zero', 'Missing']);\n});\n\nit('F8 donut: zero and null slices count toward the eight-slice limit without gaining arcs', () => {\n  const data = [\n    ...Array.from({ length: 7 }, (_, i) => ({ x: 'Slice ' + i, y: i + 1 })),\n    { x: 'Zero', y: 0 }, { x: 'Unknown', y: null },\n  ];\n  const r = chart('donut', data);\n  r.frames();\n  expect(rows(r)).toHaveLength(9);\n  expect(marks(r, 'arcs')[0]?.angles).toHaveLength(14);\n  expect(codes(r)).toEqual(['AX121']);\n  expect(r.controller.handle.diagnostics[0]?.count).toBe(2);\n  expect(lastModel(r).summary).toContain(message('otherSlices', { count: 2 }));\n});\n    'The chart palette has less than 3:1 contrast against the background. Adjust the colors or background to reach 3:1.',\n  'The chart is drawn as themed.'),\n  AX142: entry('hint', () =>\n    'The plot is too small to draw. Give the plot more room.',\n  'The chart shows the summary and table control.'),\n  AX143: entry('hint', d =>\n    field(d) + ' has ' + count(d, 'label') + ' that could not fit. Give the plot more room or shorten the labels. ' +\n    'For vertical bars with category labels, try horizontal bars (horizontal: true).',\n  'The chart shows a note that labels were hidden.'),\n  AX150: entry('warning', d =>\n    'Option ' + quote(d.field ?? '') + ' is unsupported. ' + (d.detail ?? 'Use an option supported by this chart.') + suggestion(d),\n  'The option is ignored.'),\n  AX151: entry('warning', d =>\n    field(d) + ' has out-of-order append values' + rows(d) + '. Append rows in x order at or after the last x.',\n  'The rows are accepted through a full update.'),\n  AX152: entry('warning', d =>\n    'Option ' + quote(d.field ?? 'x.timeZone') + ' has an unknown time zone' + samples(d) + '. Supply a zone recognized by Intl.',\n  'The viewer’s time zone is used.'),\n  AX160: entry('warning', d =>\n    field(d) + ' has a custom formatter that threw' + rows(d) + '. Make the formatter handle every value of this field.',\n  'The default format is used for the affected value.'),\n    code, level: diagnosticRegistry[code].level, effect: code === 'AX105' ? 'none' : effect, origin,\n    message: diagnosticRegistry[code].message({ field, rows: firstRows, count, ...context, outcome }),\n    ...(field === undefined ? {} : { field }),\n    ...(firstRows === undefined ? {} : { rows: firstRows }),\n    ...(count === undefined ? {} : { count }),\n  };\n  contexts.set(diagnostic, context);\n  return diagnostic;\n}\n\nexport function report(sink: DiagnosticSink, code: DiagnosticCode, effect: DiagnosticEffect, details?: DiagnosticDetails): void {\n  sink.add(createDiagnostic(code, effect, details));\n}\n\nit('uses the external heading when supplied, otherwise generates and reports a missing name', () => {\n  const diagnostics = new DiagnosticCollector();\n  const labelled = read(trend, { labelledBy: 'heading', caption: 'Outside heading', diagnostics });\n  expect(labelled.name).toBe('');\n  expect(labelled.table?.caption).toBe('Outside heading Reference line Target at 20.');\n  expect(read(trend, { labelledBy: 'heading' }).table?.caption)\n    .toBe('Line chart of Sessions by Day Reference line Target at 20.');\n  expect(diagnostics.inputs()).toEqual([]);\n  expect(read(trend, { diagnostics }).name).toBe('Line chart of Sessions by Day');\n  expect(diagnostics.inputs()).toMatchObject([{ code: 'AX140', effect: 'none' }]);\n  expect(read(trend, { messages: resolveMessages({ chartName: '{x} and {y} ({type})' }) }).name).toBe('Day and Sessions (Line)');\n});\n\nit('formats one requested row of a million-row table and finds its page by x', () => {\n  const size = 1_000_000;\n  const x = Float64Array.from({ length: size }, (_, i) => i * 2);\n  const duration = Float64Array.from(x, v => v / 2 + 0.5);\n  const hidden = Float64Array.from(x, v => v / 2 + 2);\n  const data = frame('line', { data: { columns: { x, duration, hidden } }, x: { field: 'x', label: 'Index' },\n    y: [{ field: 'duration', label: 'Duration', unit: 'ms' }, { field: 'hidden', label: 'Bytes', unit: 'B' }] });\n  expect(data.x.values).toBe(x);\n  const formatters = formatter(data);\n  const formatX = vi.fn(formatters.x);\n  const formatValue = vi.fn(formatters.value);\n  const view = aligned(data, { visible: [true, false] });\n  const start = performance.now();\n  const model = read(view, { title: 'Timing', formatters: { ...formatters, x: formatX, value: formatValue } });\n  expect(formatX).not.toHaveBeenCalled();\n  expect(formatValue).not.toHaveBeenCalled();\n  const table = model.table!;\n  expect(table.headers).toEqual(['Index', 'Duration (ms)', 'Bytes (B)']);\n  expect(table.rowCount).toBe(size);\n  expect(table.pageSize).toBe(100);\n  expect(table.row(900_000)).toEqual(['1,800,000', '900,000.5 ms', '900,002 B']);\n  expect(table.pageForX(1_799_999)).toBe(9000);\n  expect(table.pageForX(1_800_000)).toBe(9000);\n  expect(table.pageForX(2_000_000)).toBeNull();\n  expect(table.row(size)).toBeNull();\n  expect(formatX).toHaveBeenCalledTimes(1);\n  expect(formatValue).toHaveBeenCalledTimes(2);\n  expect(performance.now() - start).toBeLessThan(500);\n});\n\nit('limits the table to the current x range and omits it when disabled or compact', () => {\n  const table = read(trend).table!;\n  expect(table.rowCount).toBe(3);\n  expect(table.row(2)).toEqual(['3', '20', 'No data', '8']);\n  expect(table.pageForX(0)).toBe(0);\n  expect(table.pageForX(4)).toBeNull();\n  expect(read(trend, { compact: true }).table).toBeNull();\n  expect(read({ ...trend, compact: true }).table).toBeNull();\n  expect(read(trend, { table: false }).table).toBeNull();\n});\n\nit('uses the declared x and y units in aligned table headers without formatting any rows', () => {\n  const data = frame('line', { data: [{ x: 1, y: 2 }], x: { field: 'x', label: 'Distance', unit: 'm' },\n    y: { field: 'y', label: 'Time', unit: 's' } });\n  const x = vi.fn(() => 'One metre');\n  const model = read(aligned(data), { labels: { xUnit: 'm' }, formatters: { ...formatter(data), x } });\n  expect(model.table?.headers).toEqual(['Distance (m)', 'Time (s)']);\n  expect(x).not.toHaveBeenCalled();\n});\n\nit('marks an incomplete stack in its row header without changing the series cells', () => {\n  const data = frame('area', { data: [{ x: 0, a: 2, b: null }, { x: 1, a: 3, b: -1 }], x: 'x', y: ['a', 'b'] });\n  const table = read(aligned(data, { kind: 'area', stack: {\n    order: [0, 1], incomplete: Uint8Array.of(1, 0),\n    positive: [Float64Array.of(2, 3), Float64Array.of(2, 3)],\n    negative: [Float64Array.of(0, 0), Float64Array.of(0, -1)],\n  } })).table!;\n  expect(table.row(0)).toEqual(['0 (incomplete)', '2', 'No data']);\n  expect(table.row(1)).toEqual(['1', '3', '-1']);\n});\n\nit('lists up to three shown incomplete stack positions with the x formatter and the incomplete message', () => {\n  const data = frame('area', { data: [10, 20, 30, 40, 50].map(x => ({ x, a: 2, b: x === 40 ? 1 : null })),\n    x: { field: 'x', label: 'Distance' }, y: ['a', 'b'] });\n  const view = aligned(data, { kind: 'area', compact: true, visibleSlots: { start: 1, end: 5 }, stack: buildStack(data, [true, true]) });\n  const model = read(view, { formatters: { ...formatter(data), x: x => `${x} m` },\n    messages: resolveMessages({ incompleteStack: 'partial' }) });\n  expect(model.summary).toContain('Distance (partial): 20 m, 30 m, 50 m.');\n});\n\nit('counts incomplete stacks when a compact summary would need more than three positions', () => {\n  const data = frame('bar', { data: [10, 20, 30, 40].map(x => ({ x, a: 2, b: null })),\n    x: { field: 'x', label: 'Distance' }, y: ['a', 'b'] });\n  const view = aligned(data, { kind: 'bar', stack: buildStack(data, [true, true]) });\n  const formatters = { ...formatter(data), count: (n: number) => `count(${n})` };\n  expect(read(view, { compact: true, formatters }).summary).toContain('Distance (incomplete): Total count(4).');\n  expect(read(view).summary).not.toContain('incomplete');\n});\n\nit('presents grouped donut categories separately in the table and together in the summary', () => {\n  const values = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 64];\n  const data = frame('donut', { data: values.map((value, i) => ({ category: `C${i}`, value })), label: 'category',\n    value: { field: 'value', label: 'Count', unit: 'sessions' } });\n  const base = donut(data);\n});\n\nit('resolves hidden and zoomed-out scatter refs and steps from the replacement', () => {\n  const data = points([[[0, 5], [2, 3], [4, 8], [6, 1]], [[2, 99]], [[2, 4], [4, 1]]]);\n  const view = scatter(data, {\n    visible: [true, false, true], xDomain: [2, 4],\n    visiblePoints: [{ start: 1, end: 3 }, { start: 0, end: 1 }, { start: 0, end: 2 }],\n  });\n  const model = buildLookup(view, layout, formatter(data), defaultMessages);\n  expect(model.resolve(point('S1', 4, 2))).toEqual(point('S0', 1, 2));\n  expect(model.step(point('S1', 4, 2), 'next')).toEqual(point('S2', 5, 2));\n  expect(model.resolve(point('S0', 0, 0))).toEqual(point('S0', 1, 2));\n  expect(model.resolve(point('S0', 3, 6))).toEqual(point('S0', 2, 4));\n  expect(model.resolve(point('S0', 99, 2))).toEqual(point('S0', 2, 4));\n  expect(model.step(point('S0', 0, 0), 'next')).toEqual(point('S2', 5, 2));\n  expect(model.step(point('S0', 3, 6), 'previous')).toEqual(point('S2', 6, 4));\n  expect(model.step(point('S0', 2, 4), 'page-next')).toBeNull();\n  expect(model.step(point('S0', 1, 2), 'page-previous')).toBeNull();\n});\n\nit('bounds a pick in a cell of 200,000 coincident points and reports the full count', () => {\n  const size = 200_000;\n  const base = points([[]]);\n  const data = { ...base, series: [{\n    ...base.series[0]!, x: new Float64Array(size).fill(23.9), y: new Float64Array(size).fill(50), row: null,\n  }] };\n  const model = scatterLookup(scatter(data), layout, formatter(data));\n  const target = model.pick(24.1, 50);\n  expect(target).toMatchObject({ kind: 'point', count: size });\n  expect(model.primary(target!)).toEqual(point('S0', size - 1, 23.9));\n  expect(model.tooltip(target!).rows).toHaveLength(8);\n  expect(model.lastPickCandidates).toBeLessThan(3_000);\n});\n\nit('bounds the points visited for 10,000 identical marks mixed with 190,000 other points in one cell', () => {\n  const size = 200_000;\n  const copies = 10_000;\n  const base = points([[]]);\n  const data = { ...base, series: [{\n    ...base.series[0]!,\n    x: new Float64Array(size).fill(50, 0, copies),\n    y: new Float64Array(size).fill(50, 0, copies + 1),\n    row: null,\n  }] };\n  const { x: xs, y: ys } = data.series[0]!;\n  // The boundary point is exactly 0.5 px away and the rest fill the same cell beyond its own radius.\n  xs[copies] = 50.5;\n  for (let i = copies + 1; i < size; i++) {\n    const j = i - copies - 1;\n    xs[i] = 51.01 + Math.floor(j / 400) / 1000;\n    ys[i] = 50.01 + (j % 400) / 1000;\n  }\n  const axis = linearScale([0, 128], [0, 128]);\n  const model = scatterLookup(scatter(data), plot({ kind: 'xy', x: axis, y: axis }, 128, 128), formatter(data));\n  for (const [x, row] of [[50, copies - 1], [50.5, copies]] as const) {\n    const target = model.pick(x, 50);\n    expect(target).toMatchObject({ kind: 'point', count: copies + 1 });\n    expect(model.primary(target!)).toEqual(point('S0', row, x));\n    expect(model.tooltip(target!).rows).toHaveLength(8);\n    expect(model.lastPickCandidates).toBeLessThanOrEqual(12);\n  }\n});\n\nit('visits the binary-search window when switching series and locates recreated refs by x', () => {\n  const n = 80_000;\n  const data = points([Array.from({ length: n }, (_, x) => [n - x, 20] as const),\n    Array.from({ length: n }, (_, x) => [x, 20] as const)]);\n  const work = { locations: 0, seriesCandidates: 0, orderComparisons: 0 };\n  const scale = linearScale([0, n], [0, 100]);\n  let maps = 0;\n  const projection = { kind: 'xy' as const, x: { ...scale, map(x: number) { maps++; return scale.map(x); } }, y: scale };\n  const model = scatterLookup(scatter(data), plot(projection), formatter(data), work);\n  maps = 0;\n  expect(model.step(point('S0', 40_000, 40_000), 'series-next')).toEqual(point('S1', 120_000, 40_000));\n  expect(maps).toBeLessThan(20);\n  expect(work.locations).toBeGreaterThan(0);\n  expect(work.locations).toBeLessThan(20);\n  expect(work.seriesCandidates).toBeGreaterThan(0);\n  expect(work.seriesCandidates).toBeLessThan(20);\n});\n\nit('walks partial ranges with hidden series and duplicate x and y in fixture order', () => {\n  const pair = fc.tuple(fc.nat(5), fc.nat(4));\n  fc.assert(fc.property(fc.array(fc.array(pair, { minLength: 2, maxLength: 17 }),\n    { minLength: 3, maxLength: 6 }), fc.boolean(), (lists, trim) => {\n    const data = points(lists);\n    const visible = lists.map((_, s) => s !== 1);\n    const visiblePoints = data.series.map(({ x }) => ({ start: trim ? 1 : 0, end: x.length }));\n    const model = buildLookup(scatter(data, { visible, visiblePoints }), layout, formatter(data), defaultMessages);\n    const expected = data.series.flatMap((series, s) => visible[s] ? Array.from(series.x).flatMap((x, i) => i >= visiblePoints[s]!.start\n      ? [{ x, y: series.y[i]!, row: series.row![i]!, s, i }] : []) : [])\n      .sort((a, b) => a.x - b.x || a.y - b.y || a.s - b.s || a.i - b.i);\n    expect(model.count).toBe(expected.length);\n    let next = model.step(null, 'next');\n    for (const [i, row] of expected.entries()) {\n      expect(next).toEqual(point(`S${row.s}`, row.row, row.x));\n      expect(model.ordinal(next!)).toBe(i);\n      expect(model.datum(next!)?.value).toBe(String(row.y));\n      expect(model.step(next, 'previous')).toEqual(i === 0 ? null\n        : point(`S${expected[i - 1]!.s}`, expected[i - 1]!.row, expected[i - 1]!.x));\n      const distance = Math.max(1, Math.floor(expected.length / 10));\n      const page = expected[Math.min(expected.length - 1, i + distance)]!;\n      expect(model.step(next, 'page-next')).toEqual(i === expected.length - 1 ? null : point(`S${page.s}`, page.row, page.x));\n      next = model.step(next, 'next');\n    }\n    expect(next).toBeNull();\n  }), { numRuns: 60 });\n});\n\nit('uses one set of grid cells for a dense noncoincident pick and its neighbours', () => {\n  const width = 500;\n  const size = width * 400;\n  const base = points([[]]);\n  const data = { ...base, series: [{\n    ...base.series[0]!,\n    x: Float64Array.from({ length: size }, (_, i) => 20 + Math.floor(i / 400) / 100),\n    y: Float64Array.from({ length: size }, (_, i) => 48 + (i % 400) / 100),\n    row: null,\n  }] };\n  const scale = linearScale([0, 128], [0, 128]);\n  const model = scatterLookup(scatter(data), plot({ kind: 'xy', x: scale, y: scale }), formatter(data));\n  const x = 24, y = 50;\n  const { x: xs, y: ys } = data.series[0]!;\n  let expected = 0;\n  for (let i = 0; i < size; i++) {\n    if ((xs[i]! - x) ** 2 + (ys[i]! - y) ** 2 <= 0.5 ** 2) expected++;\n  }\n  const target = model.pick(x, y);\n  expect(target).toMatchObject({ kind: 'point', count: expected });\n  expect(model.primary(target!)).toEqual(point('S0', 400 * 400 + 200, x));\n  expect(model.lastPickCells).toBeLessThanOrEqual(16);\n  expect(model.lastPickCandidates).toBeLessThan(3_000);\n});\n\nit('finds next and previous by one binary successor search per series', () => {\n  const seriesCount = 500;\n  const rows = 400;\n  const base = points([[]]);\n  const data = { ...base, series: Array.from({ length: seriesCount }, (_, s) => ({\n    key: `S${s}`, label: `S${s}`, drawable: true,\n    x: Float64Array.from({ length: rows }, (_, i) => i), y: new Float64Array(rows).fill(s), row: null,\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
